  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Wiki_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bfa36fdea331abe4cb2b293833ff63a0, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 188400156672
    m_Localized: "Alter-Echo production has been retired. Gather resources on adventures or harvest crops you\u2019ve planted."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 478381752320
    m_Localized: "<link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>Buffs</color></u></link> are temporary powers. They end when their duration runs out or you return to town.\n\nComplete a slot\u2019s required quest to unlock autocasting, which starts enabled. Select the slot in <link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Buffs</color></u></link> to turn it on or off.\n\nEva\u2019s <link=\"help:cauldron\"><u><color=#EFB889>Cauldron</color></u></link> can reduce buff cooldowns."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 492340396032
    m_Localized: "Your character will enter combat automatically, and only engage enemies who get in the way! Tasks first fun later.\n\nD' = D \xD7 (1 - A / (A + N))\n\nD = incoming damage\nA = defense value (clamped to 0 or higher)\nN = constant scalar that controls diminishing returns (default = 25)\nD' = final damage taken\n\nReaching your 10th, 100th, 1,000th, and 10,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 25% bonus damage against that specific enemy.\nReaching your 25,000th, and 100,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 50% bonus damage against that specific enemy."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 512217202688
    m_Localized: 'Echoes are versions of your hero from other realities. Each has its own set of abilities.


      Combat-only Echoes seek enemies. Echoes that can gather and fight prioritize tasks, then fight when engaged. Echoes that cannot fight neither attack nor attract enemies.


      Echoes unlocked through skill milestones seek tasks for that skill. For example, a Woodcutting Echo seeks Woodcutting tasks.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 532437942272
    m_Localized: 'Use the return-to-town control during a run to retreat. Each kill adds 2% to your retreat resource bonus, shown on the control.


      If you request a return during combat, your hero finishes the fight before leaving.


      You only receive this bonus if you return alive. Dying or being reaped forfeits it; you still keep the resources already gathered.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698595295232
    m_Localized: "Your hero completes tasks automatically to gather resources. Higher skill levels help you complete them faster.\n\nTasks have minimum and maximum spawn distances. Beyond a task\u2019s maximum distance, its spawn weight falls by 90%. If all eligible tasks are beyond their maximums, their relative weights still determine how often they appear."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 505754247643136
    m_Localized: "Complete a quest\u2019s requirements, then turn it in while in town.\n\n<b>Information:</b> Read or acknowledge the quest to continue the story or tutorial.\n<b>Gathering:</b> Bring the listed resources. Turning in the quest spends them.\n<b>Kills:</b> Defeat the required enemies, then report back.\n<b>Meet:</b> Find and speak with the named NPC. Some appear only after you reach a particular distance."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3785742338113536
    m_Localized: "Carl ends your run when you reach the map\u2019s limit. See <link=\"help:statistics/general\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 General</color></u></link> for map limits.\n\nBeing reaped at the limit increases distance by 1% in River, Woods and Mines. Farmlands gives no increase. Spooky scales enemy levels with kills and has no kill cap. Some quests also increase your travel limit."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6939642239008768
    m_Localized: v1.4.3
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7986628786536448
    m_Localized: 'Dragon slaying pope

      tanty.

      Mellifas

      Latimer Cross

      MatHeadGetz

      appleguy

      AwesomePhoenix

      boiledpotato

      eli

      GLUTTONY

      Gudu

      Mentocado

      Nuclearion

      Quackers

      Rugmuk

      SaintPlays

      SCHMUGGLER

      WaringMcMarrin'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133160779776
    m_Localized: "Open <link=\"help:forge\"><u><color=#EFB889>Town \u2192 Forge</color></u></link> to craft equipment, whether you\u2019re in town or on an adventure.\n\nCrafting options:\n\n<b>Stop for Vastium:</b> Always stops if you roll a Vastium piece, even if it is a downgrade.\n\n<b>Stat Matching:</b> With this enabled, the forge will continue to work until an upgrade has the exact same stat types as your equipped piece of gear.\n\nQuality is represented by this icon: <sprite=206>\n\nThis is where you craft gear and choose the best stats for your build. \nEquipment can roll 8 different stats. Each slot guarantees one of them.\n\n<sprite=198> = Damage.\n<sprite=200> = Attack Speed.\n<sprite=199> = Crit Chance.\n<sprite=205> = Crit Damage.  \n\n<sprite=202> = Health.\n<sprite=203> = Regen.\n<sprite=201> = Defense.\n<sprite=204> = Movement.\n\n<sprite=192> = Upgrade.\n<sprite=193> = Downgrade. \n<sprite=194> = No change.\n<sprite=195> Stat is not on new item.\n<sprite=196> Stat is not on old item.\n\n<b>Weapon</b> | Guarantees <sprite=198>\n<b>Helmet</b> | Guarantees <sprite=202>\n<b>Chest</b> | Guarantees <sprite=201>\n<b>Boots</b> | Guarantees <sprite=204> which is exclusive to this slot.\n\nGear is automatically salvaged when you craft a new piece, select a different slot, or close the game.\n\nDepending on rarity you can receive up to 5 stats on a piece of gear."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133185945600
    m_Localized: "Hey guys Dev here. \n\nIf you want your names in the enemy name random pool of names then please jump into discord and ask in the EoV Chat :)\n\n\u2022 I am considering moving task unlocks to the milestone system. Quests would then provide skill xp instead of task unlocks! Let me know your thoughts."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9898115700506624
    m_Localized: "<b>Changes</b>\n\u2022 Added two new quests. For the Jam! & Gilliver's Travels.\n\u2022 Improved intro message.\n\u2022 Fixed level up alerts showing lower values than you had.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge stats Quality Equipped block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests now say \"Ready to turn in\" rather than \"Complete.\n\u2022 Added an overlay when loading a map.\n\u2022 Added a new Mix All Button.\n<b>Backend</b>\n\u2022 Updated A* to a newer version."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12027031164698624
    m_Localized: "The <link=\"help:cauldron\"><u><color=#EFB889>Cauldron</color></u></link> converts selected food into stew. You choose how much to mix; stew gained depends on the food\u2019s value and the quantity. Taste stew to receive cards using the displayed reward chances.\n\nResource cards improve gathering, enemy drops and town crop harvests for the matching resource. Their copy thresholds are 1, 25, 75, 200, 750, 1500, 3500 and 10000; yield bonuses are 1%, 2%, 3%, 5%, 7%, 10%, 15% and 20%.\n\nA resource category uses the lowest card tier among its unlocked resources. Unowned cards count as tier zero. Category tiers 1 through 8 add 2%, 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%, 30%, 40% and 50% yield to that category. Card and category bonuses add together, up to 70%. Rewards, seeds, refunds and conversions do not receive these bonuses.\n\nThese card tiers are separate from resource rarity. Buff cards improve cooldowns and power. Complete all available resource and buff collections to unlock Eternal Boons."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18915029441462272
    m_Localized: "Gathering has a small chance to raise a resource\u2019s rarity tier. Town farm harvests do not roll resource tier upgrades.\nEach tier above the first permanently increases how much of that resource you collect.\n\n\u201CI\u2019d rather keep this to myself, but here you go.\u201D \u2014 Orin\n\nTier | Bonus | Chance\n<b>Tier 1</b> - 0%\\tBase\n<b>Tier 2</b> - 10%\\t1 /1,000\n<b>Tier 3</b> - 20%\\t1 / 5,000\n<b>Tier 4</b> - 30%\\t1 / 10,000\n<b>Tier 5</b> - 50%\\t1 / 50,000\n<b>Tier 6</b> - 75%\\t1 / 100,000\n<b>Tier 7</b> - 100%\\t1 / 250,000\n<b>Tier 8</b> - 150%\\t1 / 1,000,000"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25772880722018304
    m_Localized: English (en)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255181967360
    m_Localized: Adventures & Maps
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299008
    m_Localized: "Choose <link=\"help:adventure\"><u><color=#EFB889>Adventure</color></u></link>, then a map to start a run. Your hero moves between tasks and gathers resources automatically. Each map has different resources.\n\nTo see what you\u2019ve discovered, open <link=\"help:statistics/general\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 General</color></u></link> and choose a map. Locked maps show how to learn more."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299009
    m_Localized: Farming tasks appear only in Farmlands. <link="help:quests"><u><color=#EFB889>Quests</color></u></link> and NPC encounters unlock other routes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299010
    m_Localized: Tasks & Skills
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299011
    m_Localized: "Complete tasks to earn resources and skill XP.\n\nOpen <link=\"help:skills\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills</color></u></link> and choose a skill to see its bonuses and unlocks.\n\nOpen <link=\"help:statistics/tasks\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 Tasks</color></u></link> and use Boost to make a task more common within its category. Boosting also gives that category a smaller increase in how often it appears on the map."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299012
    m_Localized: "Boosting a task does not unlock it or change which maps it appears on. Map, distance and progression requirements still apply.\n\nCombat levels unlock higher core and crystal tiers. See <link=\"help:skills/Combat\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Combat</color></u></link> for the required levels."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299013
    m_Localized: Quests
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299014
    m_Localized: "Open <link=\"help:quests\"><u><color=#EFB889>Quests</color></u></link> to view your objectives. Complete a quest\u2019s requirements, then turn it in while in town to claim the reward. Resource hand-ins spend the listed items.\n\nPinned quests appear during a run. Other quests stay in the quest list."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299015
    m_Localized: <link="help:quests"><u><color=#EFB889>Quests</color></u></link> may ask for resources, enemy kills, an NPC meeting or a tutorial action. Meeting the requirements makes a quest ready to turn in. You receive its reward when you turn it in, which you can only do in town.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299016
    m_Localized: Inventory & Equipment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299017
    m_Localized: "Open <link=\"help:inventory\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Inventory</color></u></link> to inspect your equipment and resources. Select an equipped item to see its bonuses. Your total equipment bonuses include every equipped item.\n\nCompare the stats before replacing an item: a rarer item is not always an upgrade.\n\nDuring a run, select <link=\"help:hero-stats\"><u><color=#EFB889>Stats</color></u></link> beside your health bar to see your current combat stats."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299018
    m_Localized: Discovered resources appear before undiscovered ones. Both groups use a fixed resource order.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299019
    m_Localized: Combat
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299020
    m_Localized: "Your hero fights enemies automatically, then returns to their task.\n\nSelect <link=\"help:hero-stats\"><u><color=#EFB889>Stats</color></u></link> beside your health bar during a run to see your current stats. Open <link=\"help:statistics/enemies\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 Enemies</color></u></link> to see enemy stats and your kill bonuses."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299021
    m_Localized: "Damage taken = incoming damage \xD7 {0:0.##} \xF7 (defense + {0:0.##}). Defense below zero counts as zero.\n\nRepeated kills of the same enemy unlock bonus damage against it. See <link=\"help:statistics/enemies\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 Enemies</color></u></link> for your current bonus and next milestone."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299022
    m_Localized: Reaping & Returning
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299023
    m_Localized: "<b>River, Woods and Mines</b>\nCarl ends your run at the distance limit. Being reaped at that limit increases your shared reaping distance by 1%.\n\n<b>Farmlands</b>\nCarl ends your run at the distance limit, but reaping gives no distance increase.\n\n<b>Spooky</b>\nEnemy levels rise with your kills. There is no kill cap or distance reaping limit.\n\nYou keep gathered resources and skill progress when a run ends. Return to town to turn in quests, and check the <link=\"help:run-summary\"><u><color=#EFB889>Run Summary</color></u></link> to see your gains. Map information is in <link=\"help:statistics/general\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 General</color></u></link>."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299024
    m_Localized: '<b>River, Woods and Mines</b>

      Being reaped at the distance limit increases your shared reaping distance by 1% of the effective limit reached, including distance buffs. Some quests also let you travel farther.


      <b>Farmlands</b>

      Carl ends the run at its distance limit, but being reaped gives no distance increase.


      <b>Spooky</b>

      Enemy levels rise as you get more kills. There is no kill cap or distance reaping limit.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299025
    m_Localized: Retreat Bonus
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299026
    m_Localized: 'Use the return-to-town control during a run to retreat. Each kill adds 2% to your retreat resource bonus, shown on the control.


      If you request a return during combat, your hero finishes the fight before leaving.


      You only receive this bonus if you return alive. Dying or being reaped forfeits it; you still keep the resources already gathered.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299027
    m_Localized: Your retreat bonus comes from kills in the current run and is awarded when you return alive. Dying or being reaped forfeits the bonus, but does not remove the resources already gathered.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299028
    m_Localized: Forge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299029
    m_Localized: "After meeting Ivan, open <link=\"help:forge\"><u><color=#EFB889>Town \u2192 Forge</color></u></link>.\n\n1. Smelt the required materials into ingots.\n2. Select a core to set the rarity chances and material costs.\n3. Select an equipment slot, then Craft. Each craft uses ingots and one core.\n4. Compare the result. Select Equip to replace your current item.\n\nOutside Ivan\u2019s lesson, a crafted item equips automatically if its slot is empty."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299030
    m_Localized: "<b>Salvage</b>\nReview your result before crafting again or switching slots: either action salvages an unequipped result.\n\n<b>Automation \u2014 <link=\"help:forge\"><u><color=#EFB889>Forge</color></u></link> mastery level 3</b>\nCraft Until Upgrade keeps crafting, spending materials on every attempt.\n\nStop for Vastium stops on any Vastium result, even a downgrade.\n\nWith Stat Matching on, an upgrade must also have the same stat types as your equipped item before crafting stops.\n\nSee <link=\"help:skills/Combat\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Combat</color></u></link> for core and crystal unlocks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299031
    m_Localized: Buffs
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299032
    m_Localized: "Select a buff icon to see its current effects, duration and cooldown. These values include your upgrades.\n\nOpen <link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Buffs</color></u></link> to assign buffs and manage autocasting. Complete a slot\u2019s required quest to unlock autocasting for that slot.\n\n<link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>Buffs</color></u></link> end when their duration runs out or you return to town."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299033
    m_Localized: Eva's <link="help:cauldron"><u><color=#EFB889>Cauldron</color></u></link> provides buff cards that improve power and cooldowns.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299034
    m_Localized: Cauldron
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299035
    m_Localized: "Open <link=\"help:cauldron\"><u><color=#EFB889>Town \u2192 Cauldron</color></u></link>. Mix food into stew, then taste the stew to receive cards. Check the reward chances before tasting.\n\nResource cards increase how much of that resource you gather. Buff cards improve buffs. Card levels and resource rarity tiers are separate systems."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299036
    m_Localized: "A category\u2019s tier is the lowest card tier among its unlocked resources. A card you do not own counts as tier zero.\n\nResource-card and category bonuses add together, up to 70%. They apply to gathering, enemy drops and town crop harvests. They do not apply to rewards, seeds, refunds or conversions.\n\nComplete all available resource and buff collections to unlock Eternal Boons."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299037
    m_Localized: Echoes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299038
    m_Localized: "Echoes are temporary copies of your hero that gather resources or fight enemies.\n\nOrin\u2019s realms are connected. Surges of temporal energy let Echoes of your past cross between them to help you. Helping the townsfolk lets you summon Echoes yourself.\n\nEchoes unlocked through a skill\u2019s milestones seek tasks for that skill. See <link=\"help:skills\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills</color></u></link> for milestones, or the <link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>summoning buff</color></u></link> for its effects."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299039
    m_Localized: An Echo that can both gather and fight prioritizes tasks, then fights when engaged.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299040
    m_Localized: Resource Tiers
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299041
    m_Localized: "Gathering can raise a resource\u2019s rarity tier, permanently increasing how much of it you collect.\n\nTown crop harvests receive your current tier bonus but cannot raise the tier.\n\nSeed packs do not gain rarity tiers or rarity bonuses.\n\nResource tiers, equipment rarity and <link=\"help:cauldron\"><u><color=#EFB889>Cauldron</color></u></link> card levels are separate systems."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299042
    m_Localized: Resources start at Tier 1. Each upgrade chance applies when you collect an eligible resource at the previous tier.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
