  - m_Id: 164588427254829056
    m_Localized: '<b>Farmlands</b>

      Gather crops here. Farming tasks do not appear on other maps. Carl''s distance limit does not increase when you are reaped in Farmlands.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160704
    m_Localized: "<b>Farming</b>\nHarvest crop patches in Farmlands to earn crops and Farming XP. Growing your own crops through <link=\"help:fields\"><u><color=#EFB889>Fields</color></u></link> is a separate system. See <link=\"help:skills/Farming\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Farming</color></u></link> for bonuses and unlocks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160705
    m_Localized: "<b>Fishing</b>\nGill gives you your first rod. Fishing tasks award fish and Fishing XP.\n\nSee <link=\"help:statistics/general\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 General</color></u></link> for each map\u2019s discovered resources, or <link=\"help:skills/Fishing\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Fishing</color></u></link> for bonuses and unlocks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160706
    m_Localized: "<b>Mining</b>\nMine ore to earn Mining XP. Smelt ore into ingots at the <link=\"help:forge\"><u><color=#EFB889>Forge</color></u></link>, then use them to craft equipment. See <link=\"help:skills/Mining\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Mining</color></u></link> for ore unlock levels."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160707
    m_Localized: "<b>Woodcutting</b>\nChop wood to earn Woodcutting XP. Barkley\u2019s quests lead you into the Woods.\n\nSee <link=\"help:skills/Woodcutting\"><u><color=#EFB889>Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Woodcutting</color></u></link> for unlocks, or <link=\"help:statistics/tasks\"><u><color=#EFB889>Statistics \u2192 Tasks</color></u></link> to boost task chances."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160708
    m_Localized: '<b>Ready to turn in</b>

      The star marks a quest whose requirements are met. Return to town and select Turn In to claim its reward. Resource hand-ins spend the listed items.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355008
    m_Localized: '<b>Weapon</b>

      Every crafted weapon has a damage stat. Compare its other stats before replacing your current weapon.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355009
    m_Localized: '<b>Helmet</b>

      Every crafted helmet has a health stat. Its other stats can improve offense, defense or recovery.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355010
    m_Localized: '<b>Chest</b>

      Every crafted chest piece has a defense stat. More defense reduces incoming damage, with diminishing returns.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355011
    m_Localized: '<b>Boots</b>

      Every crafted pair of boots has a movement stat, which increases travel speed. Only boots can roll movement.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355012
    m_Localized: '<b>Damage</b>

      Damage per hit, before enemy defense and other modifiers. Attack speed determines how often you hit. Critical chance determines how often you land a critical hit; critical damage determines its strength.


      Select <link="help:hero-stats"><u><color=#EFB889>Stats</color></u></link> beside your health bar during a run to see your current values.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355013
    m_Localized: '<b>Defense</b>

      Reduces incoming damage. At {0:0.##} defense you take half damage; at {1:0.##} defense you take one quarter. Defense does not prevent damage completely. See <link="help:reference"><u><color=#EFB889>Reference</color></u></link> for the formula.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355014
    m_Localized: '<b>Health</b>

      Your hero dies when health reaches zero. Equipment can increase maximum health, and regeneration restores health over time.


      Select <link="help:hero-stats"><u><color=#EFB889>Stats</color></u></link> beside your health bar during a run for your current values.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355015
    m_Localized: "<b>Carl</b>\nCarl ends your run at the map\u2019s distance limit. You keep gathered resources and skill progress.\n\nRiver, Woods and Mines gain 1% distance when Carl reaps you at the limit. Farmlands gives no increase. Spooky scales with kills and has no distance reaping limit."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355016
    m_Localized: '<b>Ingots</b>

      Smelt the listed materials into ingots. Your selected core determines which ingots a craft needs and how many. Smelting makes materials; Craft makes equipment.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355017
    m_Localized: "<b>Cores</b>\nEach craft uses one core. Your selected core sets the rarity chances and material costs. Higher core tiers unlock through Combat levels. Use the <link=\"help:forge\"><u><color=#EFB889>Forge</color></u></link>\u2019s conversion controls to upgrade cores."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355018
    m_Localized: '<b>Sword</b>

      Select Weapon, then Craft. Every weapon has a damage stat. Compare the result, then select Equip to replace your current weapon.


      Crafting again or switching slots salvages an unequipped result.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355019
    m_Localized: "Select a buff above to see its current effects, duration and cooldown below. Complete a slot\u2019s required quest to unlock autocasting for that slot."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355020
    m_Localized: "Select a buff above to see its current effects, duration and cooldown below. Complete a slot\u2019s required quest to unlock autocasting for that slot."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355021
    m_Localized: '<b><link="help:cauldron"><u><color=#EFB889>Cauldron</color></u></link></b>

      Choose food and how much to mix into stew. Taste the stew to receive cards, using the displayed reward chances. Resource cards increase gathering yield; buff cards improve buffs.


      See <link="help:reference"><u><color=#EFB889>Reference</color></u></link> for resource-card and category thresholds.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355022
    m_Localized: "<b>Task Echo</b>\nGathers resources without attacking or attracting enemies. Echoes unlocked through a skill\u2019s milestones seek tasks for that skill. <link=\"help:skills\"><u><color=#EFB889>Check the milestone</color></u></link> or <link=\"help:buffs\"><u><color=#EFB889>summoning buff</color></u></link> for its duration and abilities.\n\nThe current summon\u2019s effects, duration and cooldown are shown below."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355023
    m_Localized: "<b>Combat Echo</b>\nSeeks out enemies and fights them. Combat-only Echoes do not gather resources. An Echo that can both gather and fight prioritizes tasks, then fights when engaged.\n\nThe current summon\u2019s effects, duration and cooldown are shown below."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655340417024
    m_Localized: Patch Notes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655378165760
    m_Localized: "<b>Current development changes</b>\n\n<b>Opening and progression</b>\n\u2022 Reworked the opening quests and NPC introductions.\n\u2022 Gill leads players to the River; Barkley leads them toward the Woods.\n\u2022 Gill rewards Old Boots. Ivan supplies materials and teaches players to forge and equip their first sword.\n\u2022 Menus and tutorials appear as their systems become relevant.\n\u2022 Quests can only be turned in while in town.\n\n<b>Interface</b>\n\u2022 Redesigned the Run Summary and added a compact in-run Stats panel.\n\u2022 Inventory now shows equipped items and equipment bonuses.\n\u2022 Added drag scrolling throughout the interface.\n\u2022 Rebuilt the Library with topic navigation, reference tables, and selectable icon explanations.\n\n<b>Gameplay and fixes</b>\n\u2022 Reduced task density on the first Farmlands adventure.\n\u2022 Farming tasks appear only in Farmlands.\n\u2022 Core and crystal tiers unlock through Combat levels.\n\u2022 Fixed enemy health-bar overlays and fishing animation issues.\n\u2022 Removed leaderboards.\n\nSelect <link=\"help:reference\"><u><color=#EFB889>Reference</color></u></link> for earlier patch notes."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655378165761
    m_Localized: "<b>Earlier patch notes</b>\n\n\u2022 Added For the Jam! and Gilliver's Travels.\n\u2022 Improved the introduction message.\n\u2022 Fixed level-up alerts showing lower values than expected.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge's Quality Equipped block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests show Ready to turn in instead of Complete.\n\u2022 Added a loading overlay when changing maps.\n\u2022 Added the Cauldron's Mix All button.\n\u2022 Updated the pathfinding package."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
